summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The board authorized the chair to enter negotiations with their preferred
    candidate for the superintendent position. The decision followed a robust search
    process that narrowed the field to two finalists, and an announcement will be
    made once negotiations are complete.
- topic: Farewell to Student Representatives
  text: The board honored departing student representatives Alex Davison and Angela
    Kabisa for their dedicated service. Members praised their valuable insights, maturity,
    and courage during a challenging year, and the students thanked the board and
    community for the welcoming and valuable experience.
- topic: Top Scholars Recognition
  text: The board celebrated the South Portland High School Top Scholars of 2026 in
    a ceremony where students introduced each other. The introductions highlighted
    their impressive academic records, diverse extracurricular activities, community
    involvement, and future plans for college and careers.
- topic: FY26-27 Budget and Finance Update
  text: The Director of Finance reported that the budget was approved by the City
    Council and will go to voters on June 9th. The district's projected deficit range
    has decreased, and the city has offered up to $2 million in debt forgiveness to
    cover any remaining shortfall for the current fiscal year.
- topic: Elementary School Reconfiguration
  text: An update was provided on the Elementary Reconfiguration Steering Committee,
    confirming it is a public committee exploring options for the district's schools.
    A survey was sent to Kaler Elementary families to gather input on student placement
    for the upcoming school year, with a decision still expected by the end of May.
- topic: Public Comment on Bus Overcrowding
  text: Multiple parents, a student representative, and the SPSEA President raised
    serious safety concerns about severe overcrowding on school buses. They cited
    instances of students sitting in aisles and on laps on athletic buses and regular
    morning routes, prompting the superintendent to promise an immediate investigation.
- topic: Policy First Reads
  text: 'The board approved the first read of two policies: Policy BEDB: Agenda, and
    a new Educational Equity Policy. The equity policy, developed with the district''s
    equity committee, includes procedures for data review and will move to a second
    read at a future meeting.'
